1. SageMaker Unified Studio & Dataiku Integration

Objective

Resolve credential chain and access management challenges when connecting Dataiku to SageMaker Unified Studio using the DataZone JDBC driver and EC2 Instance Profiles.

Discussion Summary

Migration to SageMaker Unified Studio

- The organization is transitioning to SageMaker Unified Studio to centralize governance and access management.
- Previously, users connected directly to Athena, requiring permissions to be managed across multiple systems.
- The new approach routes Dataiku users through SageMaker Unified Studio to maintain project-level permissions consistently.

IAM Roles and Credential Providers

- The previous implementation successfully used static AWS credentials.
- The current implementation leverages an EC2 Instance Profile.
- When the DataZone IAM credential provider is specified in the JDBC connection string, the standard Dataiku credential chain is bypassed.
- This behavior was confirmed as expected.
- The Instance Profile is used only for establishing the initial connection.
- Query execution is performed using the DataZone Project Execution Role associated with the specified Project and Environment IDs rather than the Dataiku DSS connection role.

Security and Cross-Project Access

- Concerns were raised regarding potential cross-project access when multiple teams share the same underlying Instance Profile.
- It was confirmed that access controls can be enforced within Dataiku by:
  - Creating separate JDBC connections for each DataZone project.
  - Associating each connection with the corresponding DataZone Project ID.
  - Restricting access through Dataiku group permissions.

Decision

The team agreed that relying on DataZone Project Roles for query execution is acceptable, provided:

- The Cloud Team validates the security model.
- Dataiku permissions effectively restrict access to project-specific connection strings.

