2. Dataiku Streaming Implementation & Web App Migration

Objective

Evaluate support for Server-Sent Events (SSE) and streaming responses, particularly for LLM-based applications such as Sge.

Discussion Summary

Current Limitations

- The Sge application currently uses standard Dataiku API endpoints.
- Standard API endpoints buffer the entire response before returning it.
- Native streaming is not supported through standard APIs.

Proposed Architecture

- Migrate from standard API endpoints to a Headless Dataiku Web App.
- Headless Web Apps support streaming responses and are increasingly used for LLM applications.

Infrastructure and Performance

- No infrastructure changes are required.
- Web Apps run on the same EKS infrastructure as standard APIs.
- Horizontal scaling and auto-scaling remain fully supported.

Development Considerations

The migration introduces additional flexibility but requires custom implementation of:

- Routing
- JWT authentication and token validation
- Logging and monitoring

Additional benefits include:

- Support for custom HTTP status codes.
- Greater extensibility for future enhancements.

Decision

The team approved migrating Sge from standard API endpoints to a Headless Dataiku Web App to support streaming and improved extensibility.

