4. Model Drift Monitoring & Governance Node

Discussion Summary

Governance Node vs Automated Retraining

- Automated retraining should continue to be managed within Dataiku Flows.
- Governance Node is not intended to be the primary mechanism for retraining workflows.

Purpose of Governance Node

The Governance Node should primarily be used for:

- Monitoring model performance
- Tracking drift metrics
- Alerting stakeholders
- Providing governance visibility

Although actions can technically be triggered from Governance Node, this is not considered best practice.

Viewing Drift Metrics

- Detailed metrics are available at the artifact level.
- Users should review the active artifact version for comprehensive drift information.
- Governing the artifact may be required to access full metric visibility.

Best Practice Guidance

- Implement drift monitoring and automated retraining directly within project flows.
- Use Governance Node primarily for monitoring, alerting, and governance oversight.

